  <sys:String x:Key="UiGuide">Guide</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="UiEndpointGuide" xml:space="preserve">1. Select or create an endpoint, configure its parameters and click Open (Serial / UDP), Connect (TCP Client) or Listen (TCP Server). Click Close to stop the selected endpoint. Multiple endpoints can stay online.
2. Choose an ONLINE sender in the send panel. UDP accepts a local UDP endpoint or an external host:port as receiver; TCP Server sends to an accepted client. Reception is independent of the selected destination.
3. Sending defaults to HEX, accepting two-digit bytes separated by whitespace. Choose an encoding in the Text submenu. Line endings apply only to text. Ctrl+Enter sends. Periodic sending keeps the session, target and encoded data selected at start.
4. Traffic retains the latest 1,000 records. Pausing affects display only. Export saves retained records matching the current filter. Select a row to view its complete payload in Packet details.
5. TCP / Serial rows are received chunks, not protocol frame boundaries. Settings are stored in LocalAppData. Endpoints are never started automatically.
6. Modbus master, slave and register tables are available in the Modbus tab.</sys:String>
